=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements “$c=0$ gives an ellipse” and “$c=1$ gives a circle” are true." 13194139537071 17592186576411 true] [17592186338937 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537071 17592186576411 true] [17592186338937 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=1$ gives a line\n- **II.** $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- **III.** $c=0$ gives two lines" 13194139537071 17592186576411 false] [17592186338937 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." 13194139537071 17592186576411 false] [17592186338937 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements “$c=2$ gives a hyperbola” and “$c=0$ gives two lines” are true." 13194139537071 17592186576411 true] [17592186338946 1071 "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537071 17592186576411 true] [17592186338946 1071 "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, whic