rue. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$; $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$ only." 13194139537071 17592186576411 true] [17592186345292 1074 "- Equality I is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139537071 17592186576411 false] [17592186345293 1071 "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of